From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Eckelmann <sven@narfation.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:23:34 +0000
Subject: batman-adv: fix skb leak when hard_iface is being released

batadv_batman_skb_recv() owns the skb it is given. When the hard_iface
refcount already dropped to zero, the function jumped to err_out, which
only returned NET_RX_DROP and skipped the kfree_skb() under err_free.

To avoid a leak, free the skb before returning in this case.

Fixes: fee73a8578d3 ("batman-adv: Check hard_iface refcnt when receiving skb")
Signed-off-by: Sven Eckelmann <sven@narfation.org>
Origin: upstream, https://git.open-mesh.org/batman-adv.git/commit/?id=116616d59c0496b91a51163c3b8cdb3ebd7a6356

--- a/net/batman-adv/main.c
+++ b/net/batman-adv/main.c
@@ -427,8 +427,10 @@ int batadv_batman_skb_recv(struct sk_buf
 	 * shut down otherwise the packet may trigger de-reference errors
 	 * further down in the receive path.
 	 */
-	if (!kref_get_unless_zero(&hard_iface->refcount))
-		goto err_out;
+	if (!kref_get_unless_zero(&hard_iface->refcount)) {
+		kfree_skb(skb);
+		return NET_RX_DROP;
+	}
 
 	skb = skb_share_check(skb, GFP_ATOMIC);
 
@@ -487,7 +489,6 @@ err_free:
 	kfree_skb(skb);
 err_put:
 	batadv_hardif_put(hard_iface);
-err_out:
 	return NET_RX_DROP;
 }
 
